    "revertData": "0x796c1f0d0000000000000000000000005da97170646574339edc856f5c04b99668e27f38",
    "decoded": "AccountIsBlocked(0x5da97170646574339edc856f5c04b99668e27f38)",
    "confirms": "0x796c1f0d is the selector of AccountIsBlocked(address), the one-argument form, so the blocked address is a declared parameter ABI-encoded in the revert, not trailing detail. The zero-argument form would be 0xa4dedaeb. ATS does use the other shape elsewhere: refusing to revoke an operator that holds no KYC reverts with the zero-argument InvalidKycStatus() (0xfc855b1b) followed by the address as extra data."
